Z||000000||87ECOsomething||12-28-2001||01:39 PM||||I've got something I'd like to have built out of strong - and heat-resistant - plastic.  Where can I get this done?<P>TIA||||reg||5
Z||000001||rogergarrison||12-28-2001||02:02 PM||||your going to have to get a lot more specific. There are dozens of different plastics for different purposes. Lexan and plexiglass are 2 most universal.||||reg||1
Z||000002||87ECOsomething||12-28-2001||02:21 PM||||More specifically, I want to build a custom air box (something along the lines of the air filter enclosures found on newer model cars).||||reg||1
Z||000003||rogergarrison||12-28-2001||06:46 PM||||If your meaning top covers and things like Corvetts have, molded thermoplastic would be best. Fiberglass would prob be your best bet, should hold up OK, custom molding thermo plastics require a mold, so it would cost a small fortune. Why not modify something that already exists in junkyard. I took the intake cover off a 3800 oldsmobile, ground off the logos, filled them in and painted it with crackle finish. Looks great and really disquises the engine cause no one can figure out what it is. Some possible ones to look for are late Mercedes, BMW, vette.||||reg||1
